{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1508730-best-control-spells","id":1508730,"title":"Best Control Spells","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-18T03:30:01-07:00","id":1508730,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon10.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Best Control Spells","content":"Anyone got opinions on the best Control Spells? Not the best overall spells, Control Spells. Either for the Control enhancement, or the passive effect, either one. I'm partial to:<br /> <br /> <u>Stormwind Rider</u>, for the mobility and since the wind effects are good for pretending to be a DB.<br /> <br /> <u>Peacock Shadow Eyes</u>, because the cosmetic change is pretty. Plus its a useful social power.<br /> <br /> <u>Cirrus Skiff</u>, because a pet cloud is cute.<br /> <br /> <u>Flight of Separation</u>, because birds are fun to interact with.<br /> <br /> <u>Thunder Wolf Howl</u>, because FUS RO DAH.<br /> <br /> <u>Magma Kracken</u>, because the visuals are entertaining/intimidating and it's another good DB mask.<br /> <br /> <u>Travel Without Distance</u>, because teleportation is always better with friends.<br /> <br /> <u>Benediction of Aechgenesis</u>, because... well, I'd rather be known as a life-bringer than a life-ender. Also a good Wood DB cover, but at that point you've probably got better disguises.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T04:16:18-07:00","id":1508734,"title":"","content":"It's something that is most probably not for everyone, since i'm the first to admit it counts as more of a long term/freeform investment-XP sink of sorts than straight benefit, but i'm partial to control spells that unlock the option of Evocations, like <b><i>Wood Dragon's Claw</i></b> (also possibly much more practical as Wood DB cover than Benediction of Archgenesis) and <b><i>Incomparable Body Arsenal</i></b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T06:18:36-07:00","id":1508743,"title":"","content":"I personally like Mists of Eventide's control effect. Being able to control the dreams of people you put to sleep and make them act out those dreams is just cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1494-deranged-goblin","name":"Deranged Goblin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T17:10:28-07:00","id":1508795,"title":"","content":"Dunno about &quot;best&quot;, but Thunder Wolf Howl IS a shitload o